column7:
My views on the lumia 920 after using it for a week. I shifted to Lumia 920 after being an iPhone user for more than 3 years. One of the reasons for shifting was Windows 8 and windows phone 8. I am enjoying both on the desktop and now on the new lumia phone. The people hub is fantastic with the cool integration with facebook etc   all in one place.

  Weight is not an issue at all   felt relatively heavy when I held it first. But it is just the first reaction. You don't even notice the weight now. So many have talked already in detail about the plus and minus points of the phone. So nothing much to add there. But I need to tell a few points about the actual experience.


  There was random rebooting's while on call. Initial call to Nokia support ended with them asking me to do a hard reset. But the problem persisted and the second call ended with me going to Nokia care who updated the firmware/ software and from then on, there are no issues;


  Before doing the hard resets, i had taken the backup and if we need to restore this backup, we need to necessarily sign into the windows ID, when the phone restarts. If we do not, we will not get the option to restore it later;

  Having come from iPhone, i find the selection of words or part thereoff using the fingers a bit difficult;


  Want of applications have been said a lot. Although I could find replacements for most of the iPhone applications which i was using, certain applications for home budgeting, use of access database etc were found to be inadequate or were not available. I am sure more applications will come soon.


  However, overall I really enjoy the phone and the fantastic OS. It was definitely a worthwhile shift from iOS.


  Flipkart delivery was excellent.



   READ MORE

@Siddharth Thapa:

  1)Weight is an issue agreed but once u give 2 hours on the device , its normal , for god's sake its just an extra 50 gram max ! We humans can definitely bear that much extra weight as an offset for this beauty.

  2)Apps coming to

I was confused between two phones - Samsung Galaxy S Duos 7562 and Lumia 620. After much thinking, I bought the Lumia 620 and I am happy that I chose Lumia.


  Pros:

  1. A refreshing OS (been tired of Androids and iOS);

  2. Battery life;

  3. Speakerphone;

  4. Nokia Drive and Nokia Music;

  5. MS office;

  6. Expandable memory;

  7. Decent camera;


  Cons:

  1. Less apps - Wasn't really bothered about less number of apps in WM8 but after checking the marketplace, lots of apps which are free for iOS and Androids do not appear in the store;

  2. OS is not as user friendly as iOS. Even android appears to be easier than WM8


  The cons are OS related. Nothing negative about the phone so far.



   READ MORE

I bought this phone for my wife who wanted a very basic phone having dual SIM. Since she is not very tech savvy, she insisted on one which can be used for facebook, whatsapp and checking mails and of course does have a qwerty keyboard.


  I would recommend this phone for :

  1. Budget phone;

  2. Dual sim;

  3. Decent camera;

  4. Facebook and Whatsapp;

  5. Good looks;

  6. QWERTY keyboard.


  Go for it..till stocks last.



   READ MORE

A beautiful sturdy phone which does the basic features of a phone justice.

  Call quality is good;

  Build quality is awesome;

  Whatsapp & facebook are basic but effective;

  An for a person who hates touchscreen phones, this thing gives a huge relief.

  No issues found yet!

  FYI this might just be one of the very last models which doesnt have  touchscreen yet.



   READ MORE

